{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/C# Events.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/C# Events.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"c events c events","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/C# Events.md","fileName":"C# Events.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"C# Events","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/C# Events.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/C# Events.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"c events c events","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/C# Events.md","fileName":"C# Events.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"C# Events","heading":"C# Events","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A C# event lets one object publish that something happened while other objects subscribe handlers through delegates. The publisher raises the event without requiring knowledge of every subscriber, reducing direct coupling between participants.\n\nThe event boundary restricts outside code to subscription and unsubscription rather than arbitrary invocation. Event arguments carry details about the occurrence, and a custom event-argument type can add domain-specific data beyond the conventional sender reference.\n\nAn event lets a publisher notify subscribed handlers without hard-coding each downstream action. Multiple handlers can subscribe with `+=` and unsubscribe with `-=`, allowing notification behavior to be extended independently of the publisher.\n\nThe conventional .NET handler shape receives the publishing object and an `EventArgs` value carrying event-specific data.","tags":["baby"],"links":["C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/C# Events.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/C# Events.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"c events c events","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/C# Events.md","fileName":"C# Events.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"C# Events","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}